Flex Living – Developer Assessment Documentation

Overview
- Unified web app for manager review insights and property page display.
- Single Render service: serves the React SPA and Next.js API routes under one domain.

Tech Stack
- Frontend: React 18, TypeScript, Vite, TailwindCSS, shadcn/ui, lucide-react, TanStack Query.
- Backend: Next.js 14 (pages/api), Express server envelope to serve static SPA and mount APIs.
- Build/Deploy: Render Web Service; Node default 22.16.0, health check `/healthz`.

Architecture & Decisions
- Single-domain deployment for simplicity and alignment with assessment.
- Express serves `frontend/dist` and exposes Next.js API routes via the same server.
- Hostaway normalization: 10-point ratings converted to 5-star for UI consistency.
- Approval persistence: `data/approved_reviews.json` stores approved review IDs; APIs read/write it.
- Robust static path resolution: server looks for `frontend/dist/index.html` using both `process.cwd()` and `__dirname` to avoid path issues.
- Health endpoint: `/healthz` returns `ok` if `frontend/dist/index.html` exists; aids platform checks.

Manager Dashboard
- Filters: search, property, channel, rating bands, status (published/pending), category, date range.
- Sorting: by date, rating, channel (implemented via client-side state).
- Insights: monthly trend line (last 6 months), category averages (sorted), summary stats.
- Publishing: toggle approved/published state; persists via `POST /api/reviews/approved`.

Property Details Page
- Layout aligned with Flex Living style; review section shows only approved reviews.
- Ratings display averages and category breakdowns; channel badges (Airbnb, Booking.com, Vrbo).

API Behaviors
- GET /api/reviews/hostaway
  - Returns { status, data: { reviews, listings } }.
  - reviews: normalized entries with fields: id, listingName, type, status, channel, rating10, rating5, text, categories, submittedAt, guestName, source, approved.
  - listings: per-listing aggregates: totalReviews, avg10, avg5, categoryAverages.
- GET /api/reviews/approved
  - Returns { approvedIds } from data/approved_reviews.json.
- POST /api/reviews/approved
  - Body: { id: number, approved: boolean }. Updates persisted set and returns { approvedIds }.
- GET /api/reviews/google?placeId=...
  - Requires GOOGLE_API_KEY. If missing or no placeId, returns { status: 'disabled' }.
  - On success, returns normalized Google reviews with rating5 and derived rating10.

Deployment
- Render Build Command: npm run build:all (builds SPA and Next.js).
- Render Start Command: npm run serve (Express starts; binds to process.env.PORT).
- Health Check Path: /healthz.
- Frontend build location: frontend/dist/index.html.

Images & Favicon
- Property images: stable HD US apartment photos (Unsplash/Picsum links), avoiding blanks.
- Favicon: Flex Living symbol/wordmark URL applied in frontend/index.html.

Findings: Google Reviews
- Accessible via Places Details API; returns reviews with rating and text.
- Mapping challenges: associating Google placeId with internal listings; solved by query param.
- API key required; gracefully disabled when env is absent.

